     1	# The issuer implements the registered issuance lifecycle (2026-10-29, revised after review)
     2	
     3	> **Status: OWNER DECISION**, by the owner instance (Claude Opus 5.5). It corrects an owner defect found by the
     4	> Levadura consistency panel (finding c016, `levadura_salvaje/docs/tessera-a11-canary-scorecard.md`). Resolution S4
     5	> (`docs/V1-SERVICE-RESOLUTIONS.md:23`) and the issuer failed every request 24 hours after acceptance. The
     6	> registered lifecycle (A2.1, A2.2, A2.3, with A9.2's parameters) has no such deadline and makes "every
     7	> timely-eligible attempt ships" an obligation on the implementation (`phase-0-prereg-amendment-2.md:143-145`).
     8	> Registered text governs. No registered sentence changes; owner documents and code do. Revised the same day after
     9	> Codex's design review (`docs/reviews/issuance-lifecycle/CODEX-REVIEW.md`, IL-01 to IL-07; two prechecks failed on
    10	> the first version: it carried CF2-01's lease margin into the latch, and it called a nominal budget a bound).
    11	
    12	## What is registered
    13	
    14	- **Parameters** (A9.2; frozen profile §1): δ = 72 h, ε = 24 h, k = 6, N = 3, S = 24 h.
    15	- **Attempts** (A2.3, `:259-268`): at most N. Each has its own declared issue time. A retry that changes any
    16	  committed byte needs a fresh stamp (A9.5, `phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:295`), and its signatures are frozen
    17	  before it is stamped (A9.5, `:290-296`).
    18	- **Eligibility** (A2.1 `:91-94`; A2.2 `:220-224`; A3.7.3 `:659-673`): the attempt's own authenticated evidence for
    19	  `SHA256(A_sig)`, with the lowest qualifying height buried k = 6 deep on the pinned, linked segment (profile §7.1),
    20	  satisfies all three conjuncts: `declared − ε ≤ T`, `T ≤ declared + δ`, and `confirmed_at ≤ declared + δ`. This
    21	  is narrower than the whole `VALID_STRICT` verdict, and the remaining pre-ship checks stay separate. Rows 12.2 and
    22	  12.3 of the verifier are two of the conjuncts, not the predicate.
    23	- **Latch and expiry** (A2.1 `:150-162`): eligibility observed at or before `B = declared + δ + S` is timely. The
    24	  boundary is inclusive and "latch-winning", and a latched attempt cannot expire. Expiry applies only strictly
    25	  after B, and only to attempts with no timely-latched eligibility. Atomicity of latch against expiry is an
    26	  obligation on the implementation (A2.3). If the predicate fails at issuance time, the attempt is discarded and
    27	  re-issued, subject to N (A2.1 `:161-162`). A lag beyond S *may* be refused (A2.1 `:135-138`); refusing it is not
    28	  required.
    29	- **Refusal** (A2.3 `:265-268, :279-281`): exhausting N ends issuance in an explicit refusal, durably recorded, and
    30	  the transition that expires the final attempt records the refusal in the same step. In V1 the refusal is local and
    31	  returned by the API (A9.7 row 12; `docs/V1-CLARIFICATIONS.md` CL-03). A3's portable record, commitment and
    32	  publication are not V1.
    33	- **Budget** (A2.3 `:271-274, :288-289`): N × (δ + S), twelve days, is a *nominal* budget, "not a proven wall-clock
    34	  bound". Termination is an obligation on the implementation, not a proven liveness property.
    35	- **Window** (A9 `:422`): an attempt whose T would exceed not-after is not shipped.
    36	- **No SLA here** (A2.1 `:139-142`): a hard latency bound may enter only as a deployment-profile item with monitoring
    37	  and an explicit violation outcome. It never kills an eligible attempt.
    38	
     1	------------------------- MODULE P5cP5P6_BridgeSlack_Latch -------------------------
     2	(***************************************************************************)
     3	(* Latch variant of the slack analysis (P5cP5P6_BridgeSlack.tla) —        *)
     4	(* non-author bench contract, Codex constraint 1 (2026-07-21): "the       *)
     5	(* lifecycle decision must use — or atomically latch — B [the wall time   *)
     6	(* eligibility is reached], not the eventual execution time of Ship,"     *)
     7	(* else the interleaving scheduler can manufacture expiry despite         *)
     8	(* sufficient slack — a modeling artifact, not the clock question.        *)
     9	(*                                                                          *)
    10	(* ONE-CONJUNCT DIFFERENCE from P5cP5P6_BridgeSlack: Ship's lifecycle     *)
    11	(* guard is `burialAtWall <= declared + Delta + Slack` (timeliness        *)
    12	(* latched at the eligibility instant B) instead of                        *)
    13	(* `now <= declared + Delta + Slack` (checked at execution). Under latch  *)
    14	(* semantics an attempt whose eligibility arrived inside the envelope     *)
    15	(* may ship at ANY later wall time — the scheduler cannot expire it —     *)
    16	(* and discard semantics are ruled by B alone. The base module's          *)
    17	(* analysis invariant (defined on B) is carried UNCHANGED and was never   *)
    18	(* exposed to the artifact; what this variant adds to the checked space   *)
    19	(* is the shipped states the execution-time guard excluded (ship after    *)
    20	(* the wall envelope with timely eligibility — the PostEnvelopeShip       *)
    21	(* sanity witness).                                                        *)
    22	(*                                                                          *)
    23	(* Everything else — constants, actions, transcriptions, the L-as-        *)
    24	(* declared-assumption CORRECTION — is the base module's; see its header.  *)
    25	(***************************************************************************)
    26	EXTENDS Integers, Sequences
    27	
    28	CONSTANTS MaxTime, Delta, Epsilon, KConf, DepthK, MaxSkew, MaxBlocks, Slack
    29	
    30	ASSUME /\ Delta \in Nat /\ Epsilon \in Nat /\ MaxTime \in Nat
    31	       /\ KConf \in Nat \ {0} /\ DepthK \in Nat \ {0}
    32	       /\ MaxSkew \in Nat /\ MaxBlocks \in Nat \ {0}
    33	       /\ Slack \in Nat
    34	
    35	NoAnchor == -1
    36	NoTime   == -1
    37	
    38	VARIABLES
    39	  now, chain, declared, anchorH, pendingAnchor, shipped, shipAtWall,
    40	  burialAtWall
    41	
    42	vars == <<now, chain, declared, anchorH, pendingAnchor, shipped, shipAtWall,
    43	          burialAtWall>>
    44	
    45	BlockTimestamps == {t \in 0..(MaxTime + MaxSkew) :
