codex
The scratch TLC run confirmed a missing residual path: a timely observation can be lost when its latch write is rejected, with no invocation killed, and later sustained failed polls can end the attempt. I also found a termination issue in the in-progress revision-5.2 model: it counts only intervals in the initial operating period. If too many of those intervals are missed, later failed polls cannot fill the gaps, so the attempt can remain open indefinitely.
